Here's the solution using Steiner lines (see @below for a detailed discussion).

<details><summary>Storage</summary>We have the following killer lemma.

<u>Lemma:</u> Let  $G$  be an arbitrary point, and let  $G_2$  and  $G_3$  be the reflections of  $G$  over sides  $AC$  and  $AB$ . Define  $H_2$  and  $H_3$  similarly. Then  $(ABC)\cap(AG_2G_3)$  is the anti-Steiner point of  $HG$ .

<u>Proof:</u>

[asy]
