Actually, I have the same solution as **ksun48**. The only difference is that I used  $1$  and  $1$  instead of  $0{,}5$  and  $0{,}25$ . The tracking device still can report points on the x-axis, because the distance between this points and each of two possible rabbit's positions is at most  $1$ . So the rabbit can change the square of distance between him and the hunter from  $R^2$  to

\begin{align*}
1+\left(N-R+\sqrt{N^2-1}\right)^2&=N^2-2(N-R)\sqrt{N^2-1}+(N-R)^2&=R^2+2(N-R)\left(N-\sqrt{N^2-1}\right)&=R^2+\frac{2(N-R)}{N+\sqrt{N^2-1}}\geqslant R^2+\frac{2(N-R)}{N+N}&\geqslant R^2+\frac 1N\geqslant R^2+\frac 1{101}.
\end{align*}

The rabbit spends  $N\leqslant 101$  rounds to implement this change, so it takes at most  $101\cdot\frac{10000}{1/101}=102010000$  rounds to make the square of distance at least  $10000$ . This concludes my solution.

