Thus  $X$  is the intersection of the tangents at  $B$  and  $C$  to  $(ABC)$ . It is well known, then, that  $AX$  is a symmedian. By the **Lemma**, this implies that the circumcentre of  $PQH$  lies on the reflection of the  $A$ -symmedian over the angle-bisector, which is the  $A$ -median.**Remarks** Using the same notation, we can further show that the reflection of  $A$  over  $O$  is the orthocentre of  $\triangle AE'F'$  and that  $X$  is the midpoint of  $E'F'$ . There are also many cyclic quadrilaterals that were never used.

