<details><summary>Motivation: The Ultimate Definition Challenge. </summary>From a few minutes of experimenting, it should immediately be apparent that there only exist a unique coloring up to  $3!$  rearrangement of the three colors, and they should follow a strict pattern illustrated on the second bullet point in  $\color{red} 	extbf{	ext{Coloring Intentions.}}$  So, I spent a good 4+ hours trying to find a consistent way to prove that the coloring is consistent that way, and in retrospect, considering wild polygons might be overcomplicating it by a bit (though I ignored non-rectangular polygons.)  $ule{25cm}{1pt}$ Almost all of my attempts in devising an explicit algorithm turned into ruins, because of this  $``	ext{observation}"$  I pulled out:  $	extbf{that the coloring is highly variative}$ , since it depends heavily on the dominoes' boundary edges.
