\[\measuredangle ZES=90^\circ-\measuredangle SI_AT=\measuredangle OTS = \measuredangle OPS=\measuredangle ZPS\]
and so  $ZPES$  is cyclic too. Similarly,  $ZPFT$  is also cyclic. Consequently,
\[\measuredangle PEI_A=\measuredangle PZS=\measuredangle PZT=\measuredangle PFI_A\]
and thus  $I_AEPF$  is also cyclic. Now to finish, since  $\overline{XY}$  is the Steiner line of  $P$  with respect to  $\triangle I_AEF$ , it passes through its orthocenter, which is  $Z$ .
