ot= y_{j} $$  Among  $y_{m},y_{m+1},\ldots,y_{n}$ , consider the biggest one,  $y_{t}$ . We know  $y_{t}>y_{i}$  ( $m \leq i \leq n$ ,  $i 
ot= t$ ), thus every  $R_{i}$  ( $m \leq i \leq n$ ,  $i 
ot= t$ ) is worse than  $R_{t}$ . Also we know  $x_{t}>x_{j}$  ( $1\leq j \leq m-1$ ), thus each  $R_{j}$  ( $1\leq j \leq m-1$ ) is worse than  $R_{t}$ . So  $R_{t}$  is desired restaurant. $ lacksquare$

